==German==

===Etymology===
Teenage slang. More literally, "to get on someone's cookie". The original reference is uncertain, but is probably a playful substitution of ''Keks'' for several other words which produce the same result; for example, ''auf die {{m|de|Nerven}} gehen'' and ''auf den {{m|de|Geist}} gehen''. This is possibly related to other idioms such as {{m|de|einen weichen Keks haben}} and {{m|de|einen am Keks haben}}.

